The hotter the question, the greater weight towards grading.
A question by a student counts as 1 plus addition credit

    credit = (votes) · factor/100.

Normally a heat factor of 5% is adequate, meaning if 20 people votes a question, it's value is doubled.
You may need to adjust depending on number of participants and their engagement. ";s:14:"factorpriority";s:23:"Teacher priority factor";s:19:"factorpriority_help";s:339:"A factor to count questions without teacher priority set.
Each question counts in the sum of questions asked by a student as their priority value (1, 2 ...).
For those questions without priority (0) the specified value (as a %) is counted. <br />
A 100% factor means that a non-priority question counts just as a question with priority 1. ";s:10:"factorvote";s:17:"Heat given factor";s:15:"factorvote_help";s:681:"A factor to apply to the voting count of the students when calculating grades.
In addition to writing new questions, a student can receive participation credit by voting on questions by other students.
This credit is the number of emitted votes times this factor/100.

    credit = votes · factor/100

The factor need to be adjusted depending on the total votes a student could emit
and the weight desired for this type of participation.
For instance, if a student can emit 5 heat votes, a factor of 20% means voting for other 5 questions counts as
one question written by this student. A factor of 100% means voting for other questions counts the same as writing a new question. ";s:10:"finalgrade";s:12:"Final grade ";s:3:"for";s:11:" for site: ";s:7:"grading";s:9:"Raw grade";s:4:"heat";s:7:"Chaleur";s:9:"heaterror";s:14:"Too many votes";s:9:"heatgiven";s:10:"Heat given";s:9:"heatlabel";s:17:"Heat column label";s:15:"heatlabel_descr";s:42:"Enter a default label for the Heat column.";s:9:"heatlimit";s:18:"Heat default limit";s:15:"heatlimit_descr";s:105:"Enter a default for the number of times users can apply heat/vote, per round. Zero hides the heat column.";s:14:"heatlimit_help";s:103:"Enter a default for the number of times you can apply heat/vote, per round. Zero hides the heat column.";s:12:"heatreceived";s:13:"Heat received";s:14:"heatvisibility";s:22:"Heat column visibility";s:20:"heatvisibility_descr";s:63:"If enabled, the Heat column is visible, otherwise it is hidden.";s:19:"heatvisibility_help";s:39:"If enabled, the Heat column is visible.";s:11:"hotquestion";s:12:"Question Hot";s:23:"hotquestion:addinstance";s:50:"Possibilité d’ajouter une nouvelle question Hot";s:15:"hotquestion:ask";s:19:"Poser des questions";s:19:"hotquestion:comment";s:14:"Write comments";s:18:"hotquestion:manage";s:20:"Gérer les questions";s:25:"hotquestion:manageentries";s:28:"Voir la liste des activités";s:16:"hotquestion:rate";s:14:"Rate questions";s:16:"hotquestion:view";s:18:"Voir les questions";s:16:"hotquestion:vote";s:29:"Voter à propos des questions";s:17:"hotquestionclosed";s:33:"Cette activité a fermé le {$a}.";s:20:"hotquestionclosetime";s:17:"Date de fermeture";s:16:"hotquestionintro";s:5:"Sujet";s:15:"hotquestionname";s:20:"Nom de l’activité";s:15:"hotquestionopen";s:31:"Cette activité ouvrira le {$a}";s:19:"hotquestionopentime";s:18:"Date d’ouverture";s:2:"id";s:11:"Identifiant";s:26:"improperuseviewgradesclass";s:65:"Improper use of the viewgrades class. Cannot load the grade item.";s:15:"incorrectmodule";s:30:"Co